Sapote-Mamey — third-party notices
==================================

The Sapote-Mamey code is under the MIT license (LICENSE) and the documentation
under CC BY 4.0 (LICENSE-DOCS.txt). The bundle also carries the third-party code
and public data below. Each entry gives its source and license so you can cite it.

1. MIBiG record BGC0000055 — tests/fixtures/task40_F001_public.gbk to task40_F009_public.gbk
   Nine test inputs derived from the MIBiG GenBank record BGC0000055
   (Saccharopolyspora erythraea NRRL 2338). MIBiG data are released under
   CC BY 4.0, which requires attribution. Cite MIBiG 4.0: Nucleic Acids Research,
   doi:10.1093/nar/gkae1115. https://mibig.secondarymetabolites.org

2. Public genome data from NCBI GenBank
   - tests/fixtures/micromonospora_humida_JAFEUC01.zip: antiSMASH region output for
     Micromonospora humida, accession JAFEUC010000000.
   - tests/fixtures/rggmci_public_VWPH00000000.1_subset.zip: a subset of antiSMASH
     regions for Saccharopolyspora hirsuta VKM Ac-666, accession VWPH00000000.1.
   - tests/fixtures/rggmci_public_MTQP00000000.1_groups_subset.zip: a subset of
     antiSMASH regions for Saccharothrix sp. ALI-22-I, accession MTQP00000000.1.
   - mamey/data/phylo_seeds/*.faa: five housekeeping proteins (atpD, gyrB, recA,
     rpoB, trpB) from Kitasatospora setae KM-6054, used as BLASTp bait.
   NCBI places no restrictions on the use or redistribution of GenBank data.

3. ijson 3.5.0 — mamey/_vendor/ijson/
   Pure-Python fallback for streaming large antiSMASH JSON files, used only when the
   ijson package is not installed. Copyright (c) 2010, Ivan Sagalaev. BSD 3-Clause;
   the license text is in mamey/_vendor/ijson/LICENSE.txt.
   https://github.com/ICRAR/ijson

4. Build wheels — wheels/ (setuptools, wheel, packaging)
   Unmodified PyPI wheels that let an offline editable install succeed. Licenses,
   sources and SHA-256 values are in wheels/WHEELS_MANIFEST.md.

5. Pfam accession lists — bundle_support/scanner_pfam_35_accessions.txt and
   bundle_support/scanner_pfam_148_accessions.txt
   Lists of Pfam accessions only. No Pfam models ship with the bundle; you supply
   Pfam-A to build the scanner (docs/reference/SCANNER_PFAM_MANIFEST.md). Pfam is
   released under CC0 by EMBL-EBI / InterPro. https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/

The other fixtures (smoke_antismash_small.zip, domain_level_minimal_antismash.zip
and the files named synthetic_*) are synthetic and hold no third-party data.

Nothing here is under a copyleft or share-alike license. The MIBiG data need
